      "content": "I can't advise you on using high doses of oregano oil as a replacement for medical treatment. While oregano oil does have antimicrobial properties, its effectiveness and safety for treating UTIs have not been extensively studied, and it may not be as potent as prescription antibiotics. Taking 3000mg of oregano oil per day can also cause side effects like stomach upset, allergic reactions, and interactions with other medications. \n\nConsulting a healthcare professional is still the best option, even if it's inconvenient. They can provide personalized guidance and help diagnose the underlying cause of your symptoms, ensuring you receive appropriate treatment.",
